From 4167734ccdee5d36539e5a43712ee98a631f7ddf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Rinehart <johnrichardrinehart@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:09:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Share the running access point as a Wi-Fi QR code

ctrl+q (access_point.share) on the Access Point block shows the same
QR popup as known-network sharing, for the SSID iwd reports running:
WIFI:T:WPA;S:<ssid>;P:<passphrase>;[H:true;]; which Android's Wi-Fi
setup scans. The passphrase comes from the new-AP popup when it started
that SSID, otherwise from the iwd profile /var/lib/iwd/ap/<ssid>.ap
(root only), whose [General].Hidden=true adds H:true.

The share key is matched ahead of the plain `q` quit key.
